# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Phase 4: Execution pipe classification + substitution rules
#
# Source: bench/calib/instruction_db.py resource classes, validated by
# conflict matrix (data/calib_conflict.txt) and throughput sweep
# (data/calib_tput.txt).
#
# Pipe model (SM100a):
#   ALU    — FP32 + INT share one pipe. FADD, FMUL, FFMA, LOP3, SHF, PRMT,
#            IMAD, SEL, FSEL all contend uniformly (~5.14 cyc/pair in conflict
#            matrix). 2 cyc sustained throughput at ILP≥2.
#   BF16   — Separate pipe: HADD2, HFMA2, HMUL2, F2FP, HSETP2.
#            2 cyc sustained at ILP≥2 (F2FP), 3 cyc at ILP=2 (HADD2/HFMA2).
#   FAST_INT — IADD3, LEA, MOV. Essentially free: IADD3 × anything ≈ max of
#            the two, not sum. 2 cyc standalone, merges pairs (sass_ratio=0.5).
#   MEM    — STS, LDS. Shared SMEM port. 32 cyc STS throughput, 4 cyc LDS.
#   TMA    — UTMASTG, UTMALDG, UTMACMDFLUSH. Separate TMA engine, not LSU.
#   BARRIER — BAR, BSSY, BSYNC, WARPSYNC, MEMBAR, FENCE, DEPBAR, SYNCS.
#            Control flow, not pipelined compute. Not a throughput bottleneck.
#   TMEM   — LDTM (tcgen05.ld). Separate TMEM port, ~25 cyc latency.
#   CONTROL — BRA, EXIT, NOP, CALL, RET, YIELD, ELECT, etc. No pipe cost.
#   SPECIAL — REDUX (44 cyc), VIADD (10 cyc), MUFU, S2R, CS2R. Rare.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

